        <notes>
            <note>This is most often found as a second part of Académie Universelle des Jeux,
                but Levy [2210] is only the whist translation, stitched, as issued. In that copy,
                gathering E is missigned 'D' and pages 57 and 58 are misnumbered 75 and 85. There 
                is another versions dated 1765. I have seen photographs of a few openings only and it 
                appears to be in part the same setting of type, but for some pages different type.</note>
            <note rend="paragraph"/>
            <note>Translation "B" as described in Thierry Depaulis, "Hoyle Abroad, II: Hoyle in French" in </note>
            <note rend="italic">The Playing Card</note>
            <note>, Volume 43, Number 4, page 226.</note>
        </notes>
